The '''22 Octubre Bridge''' ({{langx|bl|Ponte 22 Octubre|4=22nd of October Bridge}}, {{IPA|bl|ˈpon.te bin.tiˈdos okˈtu.bre}}) is a {{convert|8|km||0|abbr=on}} long combined [[W:List of road–rail bridges|railway and motorway]] [[W:Cable-stayed bridge|cable-stayed bridge]] spanning the [[Guadalquivir]] to connect the [[Regions of Balisca|regions]] of [[Luzamontaña]] on the south shore and [[Piedmont]] on the northern shore.

The date "22 Octubre" in the official name commemorates the accession of the [[Maroon Confederacy]] (as [[Araucaria]]) to the confederation at the [[1883 Confederal Convention]]. Araucaria's accession marked the unification of the entirety of the [[Baliscan archipelago]] under a [[Baliscan nationalism|single state]] for the first time in history. 

